  "summary": "Implemented lower.convert JSONL event importer in lower.py (stdlib json/re/datetime only, no upper/CSV import, no global mutable state). Splits on physical newlines (strips trailing CR), skips blank lines while keeping one-based physical line numbers; invalid JSON (incl. NaN/Infinity constants) -> invalid_json; non-object, missing/non-string/empty id or timestamp, or missing payload -> invalid_event; timestamp must match YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS[.frac](Z|+-HH:MM|+-HHMM) and be a valid date/offset, else invalid_timestamp (naive rejected); normalized to UTC YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ (fractions truncated, fixtures have none); first valid id accepted, later duplicate_id; invalid events do not reserve ids; order preserved; empty input gives empty lists. Local test_lower.py run: 7 tests OK.",
